---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import feed from '../data/world.json';
const data = feed as {updated_at:string|null; articles:Array<{title:string,url:string,source:string,published_at:string}>;sources:Array<{source:string,status:string,items:number}>};
const articles = data.articles || [];
const sources = [...new Set(articles.map(x=>x.source))];
---
<Layout title="Global Cyber News & Threat Reports | CyberIntel" description="Latest attributed cyber threat reports, advisories and headlines from curated independent sources.">
 <div class="shell">
 <section class="hero"><span class="tag">GLOBAL CYBER WATCH • CURATED SOURCES</span><h1>What's happening <span class="accent">in cyber?</span></h1><p>Latest published headlines from cybersecurity outlets and public advisories. Each item links to its original publisher. This is a periodic feed snapshot, not breaking-news coverage.</p><p class="muted">Last successful collection: {data.updated_at ? new Date(data.updated_at).toLocaleString('en-GB',{dateStyle:'medium',timeStyle:'short',timeZone:'UTC'})+' UTC' : 'Awaiting first collection'}</p></section>
 <section class="section"><div class="stats"><div class="stat"><div class="eyebrow">Articles indexed</div><strong>{articles.length}</strong><small>Recent curated headlines</small></div><div class="stat"><div class="eyebrow">Sources in snapshot</div><strong>{sources.length}</strong><small>Not all sources may be available</small></div><div class="stat"><div class="eyebrow">Refresh interval</div><strong>6h</strong><small>Subject to source availability</small></div></div></section>
 <section class="section"><div class="panel"><div class="panel-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">Latest coverage</div><h2>Threat reports & news</h2></div><div class="toolbar"><input id="newsSearch" type="search" placeholder="Search headlines" aria-label="Search headlines"/><select id="sourceFilter" aria-label="Filter by publisher"><option value="">All publishers</option>{sources.map(s=><option value={s}>{s}</option>)}</select></div></div><div id="newsItems" class="news-list">{articles.map(a=><article class="news" data-source={a.source} data-title={a.title.toLowerCase()}><div class="source">{a.source} · {new Date(a.published_at).toLocaleDateString('en-GB',{dateStyle:'medium',timeZone:'UTC'})}</div><h3><a href={a.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{a.title} ↗</a></h3></article>)}</div>{articles.length===0 && <div class="empty"><p>No articles collected yet. Run the GitHub Actions workflow to retrieve the first feed snapshot.</p></div>}<p id="emptyFilter" class="empty" style="display:none">No headlines match your filters.</p></div></section>
 <section class="section"><div class="panel empty"><h2>Source health</h2><div class="source-status">{(data.sources||[]).map(x=><div><strong>{x.source}</strong><span>{x.status === 'ok' ? `${x.items} recent items` : 'Source unavailable; cached items may be shown'}</span></div>)}</div><p>CyberIntel republishes headline metadata only. Publishers retain copyright to their reporting. Feed access, update times and completeness vary. Always verify emerging incidents at the original source.</p></div></section>
 </div>
 <script>
 const search=document.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('#newsSearch');const filter=document.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('#sourceFilter');const nodes=[...document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.news')];const empty=document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#emptyFilter');function update(){let count=0;for(const node of nodes){const visible=(node.dataset.title||'').includes((search?.value||'').trim().toLowerCase())&&(!filter?.value||node.dataset.source===filter.value);node.hidden=!visible;if(visible)count++;}if(empty)empty.style.display=count===0&&nodes.length>0?'block':'none'}search?.addEventListener('input',update);filter?.addEventListener('change',update);
 </script>
 <style>.news-list{display:grid}.news{padding:21px 24px;border-bottom:1px solid #293950}.news[hidden]{display:none}.news h3{margin:8px 0 0;font-size:18px;line-height:1.4}.news .source{font-size:12px;color:#65d7cc}.news a:hover{text-decoration:underline}.source-status{display:grid;gap:10px;margin:20px 0}.source-status>div{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;padding:12px;background:#10263a;border-radius:8px;flex-wrap:wrap}.source-status span{color:#aabacf}.empty{padding:24px}.panel-head h2{margin:8px 0}</style>
</Layout>
